      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out the main point of the given passage. Let me read through it again to make sure I understand it correctly.\n\nThe context talks about inflation's effect on purchasing power. A retired scientist and her family have saved money for decades, but inflation has reduced their savings to only enough to buy a kilogram of sausages. This makes them feel angry and consider breaking the law. The passage then connects this to a broader societal issue: when many people feel this way, the moral level of society decreases, leading to instability.\n\nNow, the question is asking which option is the main point of the passage. The options are A, B, C, or D.\n\nLet me go through each option one by one.\n\nOption A: Inflation will do great harm to the interests of honest workers. The passage mentions a retired scientist and an honest worker, but it's more about how inflation affects their savings and leads to moral issues rather than directly stating harm to their interests. So maybe A is partially correct but not the main point.\n\nOption B: If the workers in the city suffer unfair losses, it is easy to break the law. The passage does mention that the honest worker feels angry and might break the law, but it's more about the societal impact than the direct consequence of suffering losses. It's a part of the effect, but not the main point.\n\nOption C: Inflation will greatly lower the living standard of honest workers. The passage does talk about reduced purchasing power and how it affects their savings, which relates to their living standards. However, the main point seems to be about the societal impact rather than just the personal effect on living standards.\n\nOption D: One of the serious consequences of inflation is to undermine social stability. The passage explicitly states that when many people feel unfairly treated, the moral level drops and society becomes unstable. This seems to be the main consequence mentioned.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the main point is about the societal impact of inflation leading to instability, which is option D.\n</think>\n\nThe main point of the passage is that inflation leads to a decrease in societal moral levels and instability. \n\n**Answer: D**",
