      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out the main meaning of the given passage and choose the correct option from A to D. Let me read the passage again carefully.\n\nThe passage starts by saying that reason is the most reliable tool when people need to make reliable judgments in complex situations. It mentions that irrational tools like hunches and habits are sometimes used, but relying on reason is the easiest way to succeed when it's important or when success depends on the judgment made. It also talks about established methods and principles that help determine what's appropriate and true, guiding us to draw inferences from what we know.\n\nNow, looking at the options:\n\nOption A says, \"Reason is the most reliable tool for people to make judgments.\" That seems to align with the first part of the passage, which emphasizes reason as the most reliable tool.\n\nOption B states, \"Now there is a set of methods that can help people make reliable judgments.\" The passage mentions \"some reasonable methods that have been tested for a long time,\" but it doesn't specify that \"now\" there is a set, so I'm not sure if \"now\" is the right word here. It might be more about the existence of methods rather than it being a recent development.\n\nOption C claims, \"Irrational tools cannot be trusted when people need to make reliable judgments.\" The passage does say that irrational tools like hunches and habits are often used, but it doesn't explicitly say they cannot be trusted. It just mentions that reason is more reliable.\n\nOption D says, \"A rational judgment of a complex situation will not be wrong.\" The passage doesn't make any absolute statements about rational judgments always being correct. It just says reason is reliable and established methods help, but it doesn't guarantee that a rational judgment won't be wrong.\n\nSo, the main point is that reason is the most reliable tool for making judgments, which is option A. The other options either misrepresent the passage or don't capture the main idea as clearly.\n</think>\n\nThe main meaning expressed in the passage is that reason is the most reliable tool for making judgments. \n\n**Answer: A**",
