heir financial benefits. So option C.\n\nBut wait, option B is about whether the process (faster and accurate) will benefit financially. So both are about financial benefits, but the way they argue it is different.\n\nHmm, perhaps the correct answer is C because it's about the action of switching, which is more directly the point of contention. Zhang says it's good for profits, Li says it's bad.\n\nAlternatively, option B is about the process's characteristics leading to financial benefits, which is also a point Zhang makes.\n\nWait, the question is about the difference of opinion, so it's about the specific points they disagree on. So both B and C are about financial benefits, but perhaps the exact wording is important.\n\nLooking back, option B says whether a faster and accurate process will benefit financially. Zhang says yes, Li says no. So that's a direct difference.\n\nOption C is whether switching to electronic will benefit financially. Zhang says yes, Li says no. So both B and C are correct, but the options are A, B, C, D, so only one is correct.\n\nWait, the options are:\n\nA) Faster and accurate vs manual\n\nB) Faster and accurate process benefits financially\n\nC) Switching to electronic benefits financially\n\nD) For most customers, electronic seems indifferent and inhumane.\n\nSo the main disagreement is about whether switching to electronic will help financially. So C is the difference.\n\nBut wait, the question is about the difference of opinion, so it's about the specific points they disagree on. So both B and C are about financial benefits, but perhaps the correct answer is C because it's about the action of switching, which is more directly the point.\n\nAlternatively, the question might be looking for the specific aspect. Since Zhang mentions that using electronic procedures will increase profits because orders enter queues faster, while Li says it will reduce income because people prefer calling. So the core difference is whether switching to electronic will benefit financially. So option C.\n\nBut I'm a bit confused because both B and C are about financial benefits. Let me read the options again.\n\nOption B: Whether a faster and more accurate ordering process will benefit their financial benefits.\n\nOption C: Whether switching to an electronic order process will benefit their financial benefits.\n\nSo both are about financial benefits, but the process in B is about the characteristics, while in C it's about the action of switching.\n\nIn the context, Zhang says using electronic (switching) will increase profits because it's faster and accurate. So the main point is that switching (which involves a faster and accurate process) will benefit financially. So the difference is about whether switching (which includes faster and accurate) will help financially.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.\n</think>\n\nThe difference of opinion between Zhang Qiang and Li Ming revolves around whether switching to an electronic order process will benefit their financial benefits. Zhang supports it, while Li opposes it. \n\n**Answer: C**",
