      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out which option best supports the given statement about Shell oil company. Let me start by reading the context again carefully.\n\nThe context says that Shell ranks first in total net profit among 500 major companies for three consecutive years because it has a lot of international business. So the main reason given is their international business.\n\nNow, the question is asking which option, if true, best supports this statement. Let's look at each option one by one.\n\nOption A: The profits of oil companies with the same scale as Shell but less international business are lower than Shell's. Hmm, this seems relevant because it's comparing Shell's performance with similar companies that don't have as much international business. If these companies have lower profits, it would support the idea that Shell's international business is a key factor in their success. So this could be a good candidate.\n\nOption B: In history, the champion of the net profit of the world's 500 major companies is oil companies. This is talking about historical performance, not specifically about Shell's situation over the past three years. While it's true that oil companies often top the list, the context is about why Shell specifically has been first for three years. So this might not directly support the given statement as well as another option might.\n\nOption C: Over the past three years, the world's 500 largest companies have been trying to move towards internationalization. This is about the trend of companies moving international, but the context is about Shell's success due to their existing international business. It doesn't directly link to why Shell is successful, so maybe not the best fit.\n\nOption D: In the past three years, the prices of oil and refined oil have been very stable. This relates to the oil industry but doesn't directly explain why Shell's international business is the reason for their high profits. If prices were stable, maybe other companies would also benefit, so it might not specifically support Shell's success due to their international business.\n\nSo, comparing the options, A seems to directly support the statement by showing that companies without as much international business as Shell have lower profits. This aligns with the reasoning in the context. Option B is true but doesn't tie directly to Shell's success in the specific timeframe mentioned. Options C and D are less relevant to the main point.\n</think>\n\nThe correct answer is A.\n\n**Answer: A**",
