00,000. So each year, the salary increases by $200,000. So after the first year, it's $1.2 million, and after the second year, it's $1.4 million. So over two years, the total salary would be $1 million + $1.2 million = $2.2 million.\n\nComparing that to Huizhong's total of $1.05 million over two years, Cantor's offer is better. But wait, maybe I'm miscalculating. Let me check again.\n\nHuizhong's offer is a half-year salary of $500k, increasing by $50k each half-year. So over two years, that's four half-years. Each half-year, the salary increases by $50k. So the first half-year: $500k, second: $550k, third: $600k, fourth: $650k. So total over two years would be $500k + $550k + $600k + $650k = $2,300,000.\n\nWait, no, that's over four half-years, which is two years. So total is $2,300,000.\n\nCantor's offer is $1 million annually, increasing by $200k each year. So over two years, it's $1 million + $1.2 million = $2.2 million.\n\nSo Huizhong's total is higher at $2.3 million compared to Cantor's $2.2 million. So David would prefer Huizhong because he gets more money over two years.\n\nWait, but the options are about the extra money. Let me see the options again.\n\nOption A: David will go to Cantor because he gets an extra $150k in two years.\n\nOption B: David will go to Huizhong because he gets an extra $50k a year.\n\nOption C: David will go to Cantor because he gets an extra $50k a year.\n\nOption D: David will go to Huizhong because he gets an extra $70k a year.\n\nWait, so I need to calculate the extra money each option is talking about.\n\nLet me calculate the total salary for each company over two years.\n\nHuizhong:\n\n- Year 1 (two half-years): $500k + $550k = $1,050k\n\n- Year 2: $600k + $650k = $1,250k\n\nTotal over two years: $1,050k + $1,250k = $2,300k\n\nCantor:\n\n- Year 1: $1,000k\n\n- Year 2: $1,200k\n\nTotal over two years: $2,200k\n\nSo over two years, Huizhong pays $2,300k, Cantor pays $2,200k. So David would choose Huizhong because he gets more money.\n\nNow, let's see the options.\n\nOption B says David goes to Huizhong because he gets an extra $50k a year. Let's see: The difference between Huizhong and Cantor over two years is $100k ($2,300k - $2,200k = $100k). So over two years, David gets an extra $100k with Huizhong.\n\nBut the options are talking about per year or in two years.\n\nOption B says extra $50k a year. So over two years, that's $100k, which matches the difference. So David would choose Huizhong because he gets an extra $50k per year, totaling $100k over two years.\n\nOption D says he gets an extra $70k a year, which doesn't make sense because the difference is $100k over two years, so $50k per year.\n\nOption A says he gets $150k in two years, which is more than the actual difference.\n\nOption C says he goes to Cantor for $50k a year, which is incorrect because Cantor pays less.\n\nSo the correct answer is B: David will go to Huizhong because he will get an extra $50,000 a year.\n</think>\n\nThe correct answer is B. David chooses Huizhong because over two years, he receives an extra $50,000 per year compared to Cantor.\n\n**Answer: B**",
