te of what Lance concludes. I don't think so. Frank isn't saying that experience teaches that every rule has exceptions is wrong, but rather that it leads to a contradiction.\n\nC) Showing that Lance's conclusion involves him in a contradiction. Yes, that seems right. Frank's argument creates a contradiction, so he's showing that Lance's conclusion can't hold because it leads to an impossible situation.\n\nD) Showing that it has no implications for any real cases. I don't think so. Frank's argument is about logic, not real cases specifically.\n\nSo, the correct answer should be C. Frank is showing that Lance's conclusion leads to a contradiction, thus countering it.\n</think>\n\nC) Showing that lance's conclusion involves him in a contradiction",
