ons that the latest closed furnaces are extremely fuel-efficient. The Plant Manager didn't talk about fuel efficiency, only about the cost of equipment and the higher running costs. So the Supervisor is disagreeing with the Plant Manager on this point, which the Plant Manager didn't address.\n\nWait, but the Plant Manager did talk about the cost of installing new equipment, but the Supervisor is pointing out that closed furnaces are more fuel-efficient, which the Plant Manager didn't mention. So the disagreement is about the fuel efficiency of the closed furnaces, which the Plant Manager didn't consider, thinking only about the cost and lack of profit.\n\nSo the point of disagreement is D: Whether closed copper-smelting furnaces are more fuel-efficient than open furnaces.\n</think>\n\nThe supervisor disagrees with the plant manager's point about the cost of the new process, specifically regarding the fuel efficiency of closed furnaces. \n\n**Answer: D**",
