verse feelings. So C might be related but not the strongest fit.\n\nOption D: \"Repeated playback of the same ad will cause tv viewers to get bored or even angry, and thus have a strong antipathy to the products that the merchant is trying to promote.\" This directly addresses the negative effects of repeating ads, causing boredom, anger, and antipathy towards the products. That aligns perfectly with the context which mentions negative effects and economic trouble. So D seems to best emphasize the argument.\n\nWait, let me double-check. The context says that repeating ads is unwise because it doesn't achieve the desired purpose and has a negative effect. D is talking about viewers getting bored or angry, leading to antipathy towards the products. That's exactly the negative consequence mentioned. So yes, D is the best option.\n</think>\n\nThe correct answer is D. It directly addresses the negative effects of repeated ads, aligning with the context's argument about their ineffectiveness and negative impact.\n\n**Answer: D**",
